Docker Learning Notebook

1. Verify Docker Installation

docker ps

Purpose
Displays the list of currently running Docker containers.
---

2. Refresh Docker Group Permission

newgrp docker

Purpose

Applies Docker group permission changes without logging out and back in.
---

# Working with Docker Images

3. Pull Alpine Linux Image

docker pull alpine:3.22.4

Purpose

Downloads the lightweight Alpine Linux image from Docker Hub.
---

5. List Downloaded Images


docker images

Purpose

Displays all Docker images available locally.
---

6. Pull BusyBox Image

docker pull busybox:stable-uclibc

Purpose

Downloads the BusyBox lightweight Linux utility image.
---

Running Containers

7. Run Alpine Container

docker run alpine:3.22.4

Purpose

Starts a temporary Alpine Linux container.

Note

Since no command is provided, the container starts and exits immediately.
---

8. Check All Containers


docker ps -a


Purpose

Shows both running and stopped containers.
---

9. Run Nginx Container


docker run nginx


Purpose

Runs an Nginx web server container.

Note

Without port mapping, the website is not accessible from the browser.

---

# Port Mapping in Docker

10. Run Nginx with Port Mapping

docker run -p 80:80 nginx

Purpose

Maps:

* Host Port → 80
* Container Port → 80

Access Website


http://SERVER_IP
---

11. Port Conflict Example


docker run -p 80:80 nginx


Possible Error

Port `80` is already in use by another service or container.
---

# Using Alternative Ports

12. Run Nginx on Custom Port


docker run -p 8089:80 nginx


Purpose

Maps:

* Host Port → 8089
* Container Port → 80

Access Website


http://SERVER_IP:8089
---

Detached Mode

13. Run Nginx in Background


docker run -d -p 8089:80 nginx


 Options Used

| Option | Meaning                                   |
| ------ | ----------------------------------------- |
| `-d`   | Run container in detached/background mode |
| `-p`   | Port mapping                              |

---

Important Docker Commands Summary

| Command                                | Description                 |
| -------------------------------------- | --------------------------- |
| `docker ps`                            | List running containers     |
| `docker ps -a`                         | List all containers         |
| `docker images`                        | List images                 |
| `docker pull <image>`                  | Download image              |
| `docker run <image>`                   | Run container               |
| `docker run -d <image>`                | Run container in background |
| `docker run -p HOST:CONTAINER <image>` | Port mapping                |
